# Cargo Upwell

Cargo Upwell is the optional tooling companion to the framework. It discovers application targets, builds isolated probes, validates canonical tooling documents, exposes those operations as a Rust API, and renders selected command projections. It never starts the application server.

## Choose a task

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| install the command, validate a target, inspect resources, automate reports, or configure completion | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/cli">CLI</GuideRef> |
| run discovery, probes, `check`, or `doctor` from Rust | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/programmatic-api">Programmatic API</GuideRef> |
| define template sources, metadata-only tools, or renderer registration | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/catalog">Catalog</GuideRef> |
| implement, build, sandbox-test, and diagnose an executable renderer guest | <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/renderers">Renderers</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Start with a valid application from <GuideRef slug="getting-started">getting started</GuideRef>. Keep the installed Cargo Upwell release compatible with the application, use explicit package and binary selection in automation, and preserve canonical JSON or envelopes whenever presentation output may omit evidence.

Catalog owns registration and selection metadata. Renderers owns only executable guest implementation and failure behavior; it links back to catalog rather than restating entry precedence and collision rules.
